LOCAL PATCH (not submitted anywhere): media: hisilicon: add the Hi3798CV200 VDEC and VPSS V4L2 drivers

Port of the out-of-tree HiSilicon Hi3798CV200 video decoder (histb-vdec) and
video post-processing engine (histb-vpss) from the community Linux 6.12 tree
(github.com/HiSilicon-Development/linux-6.12.y @ 79347a39f, GPL-2.0-only) to
Linux 6.18.55 AArch32 (multi_v7, no LPAE).

VDEC: stateless H.264, HEVC (Main/Main10), MPEG-2, VP8, VP9 (Request API) and
stateful MPEG-4 Part 2 / VC-1 Annex G+L / H.264 MVC.  VPSS: tile->linear
conversion, scaling, field-rate deinterlace.  Both build as modules.

Differences from the 6.12 source:
  * AVS/AVS+ support is NOT carried.  It needs a non-upstream V4L2 uAPI
    (V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS_SLICE, V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS_*, v4l2_ctrl_avs_*) added
    to videodev2.h/v4l2-controls.h/v4l2-ctrls-core.c in the 6.12 tree, and it
    is the only user of the VDH MMU identity table and of histb-avsp.bin.
    All of that code (about 1,600 lines) is removed; every other codec runs
    with the VDH MMU in bypass exactly as before.
  * v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish_states() - a core helper the 6.12 tree
    added - is added to v4l2-mem2mem.c/.h; the existing
    v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish() becomes a wrapper.  It lets a decoder
    complete the OUTPUT and CAPTURE buffer with different vb2 states.
  * 6.18 API: platform_driver .remove_new -> .remove, v4l2_fh_add()/del()
    take the struct file, MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string.
  * 32-bit: two 64-bit divisions would have pulled in __aeabi_uldivmod /
    __aeabi_ldivmod, which the ARM kernel does not provide (the module would
    not load): VP9 scale factor -> div_u64(), MPEG-4 GMC rounding -> div_s64().
    The VC-1 BPD timeout was computed as 4000 * NSEC_PER_MSEC in a 32-bit long
    (overflowed negative, so the timeout test could never fire) -> (u64) cast.
  * One -Wparentheses warning fixed (VP9 picture message).
  * HIGHMEM: dma_alloc_noncoherent() is page_address(dma_alloc_pages()), which is
    NULL for a highmem page - the call fails AND leaks the contiguous block.
    The Q10 Pro runs CONFIG_HIGHMEM=y with 2 GB RAM and a 3G/1G split, so its
    CMA area (0x76800000) is in highmem.  New histb-dma.h maps such blocks with
    vmap(); the 5 allocation sites (decoded tile/PMV surfaces, cacheable
    capture buffers, VPSS staging buffer) use it.
  * Kconfig/Makefile for drivers/media/platform/hisilicon/ (VDEC + VPSS only;
    the 6.12 tree's DMX/JPGE/VENC are not ported) and the two DT bindings.

Needs the CABAC tables at run time (request_firmware_direct):
  /lib/firmware/hisilicon/histb-h264-cabac.bin   (5120 bytes)
  /lib/firmware/hisilicon/histb-hevc-cabac.bin   (928 bytes)
Needs the CRG clocks of 0009-clk-hisilicon-crg-hi3798cv200-vdec-vpss-clocks.patch
and the nodes of vdec-dt-snippet.dtsi.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-vdec.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-vdec.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..71c4d0e65
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-vdec.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/media/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-vdec.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: HiSilicon Hi3798CV200 video decoder
+
+maintainers:
+  - linux-media@vger.kernel.org
+
+description:
+  The Hi3798CV200 video decoder contains a video decoding hardware engine,
+  stream code detector, bit-plane decoder and a local memory management unit.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: hisilicon,hi3798cv200-vdec
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    items:
+      - description: Video decoding hardware interrupt
+      - description: Stream code detector interrupt
+      - description: Decoder memory management unit interrupt
+
+  interrupt-names:
+    items:
+      - const: vdh
+      - const: scd
+      - const: mmu
+
+  clocks:
+    items:
+      - description: Video decoding hardware clock
+      - description: Video decoder DSP clock
+      - description: Bit-plane decoder clock
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: vdh
+      - const: dsp
+      - const: bpd
+
+  resets:
+    items:
+      - description: Video decoding hardware reset
+      - description: Stream code detector reset
+      - description: Main format decoding engine reset
+      - description: Bit-plane decoder reset
+
+  reset-names:
+    items:
+      - const: vdh
+      - const: scd
+      - const: mfd
+      - const: bpd
+
+  memory-region:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      Optional dedicated shared-dma-pool for decoder surfaces and working
+      buffers. It has to lie inside the DMA aperture of the SoC bus.
+
+  hisilicon,vpss:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description: Video post-processing engine used for tile-to-linear output
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+  - interrupt-names
+  - clocks
+  - clock-names
+  - resets
+  - reset-names
+  - hisilicon,vpss
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/histb-clock.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
+
+    video-codec@f8c30000 {
+        compatible = "hisilicon,hi3798cv200-vdec";
+        reg = <0xf8c30000 0x10000>;
+        interrupts = <GIC_SPI 95 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+                     <GIC_SPI 104 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+                     <GIC_SPI 149 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+        interrupt-names = "vdh", "scd", "mmu";
+        clocks = <&crg HISTB_VDH_CLK>,
+                 <&crg HISTB_VDH_DSP_CLK>,
+                 <&crg HISTB_BPD_CLK>;
+        clock-names = "vdh", "dsp", "bpd";
+        resets = <&crg 0x78 4>, <&crg 0x78 5>,
+                 <&crg 0x78 6>, <&crg 0x88 4>;
+        reset-names = "vdh", "scd", "mfd", "bpd";
+        hisilicon,vpss = <0x1>;
+    };
